@prefix sh:   <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix tss:  <https://w3id.org/tss#> .
@prefix emb:  <https://w3id.org/tss/shapes/embedded#> .

# =============================================================================
# TSS conformance shapes for EMBEDDED data: a source whose points are inside the metadata
# itself. Its class says how they are written:
#
#   tss:EmbeddedRDFSource: the points are RDF. Each point is one reading of one value field, a
#   node of its own, linked from its source with tss:hasPoint. It states its value field
#   (tss:field), its time (tss:time) and its reading (tss:value), and the values of the
#   describing fields that describe its value field, each with the tss:property of that
#   describing field; each value is a literal typed by its field's tss:datatype, e.g.
#     ex:zevenaarshaven-source tss:hasPoint [
#         tss:field ex:zevenaarshaven-ec20-value-field ;
#         tss:time "2021-03-03T23:15:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
#         tss:value "4797.72"^^xsd:double ;
#         ex:qualityCodeColor "rgba(0, 128, 0, 1.0)"^^xsd:string
#     ] .
#   A point of a source with one value field may leave out tss:field. The points of one time
#   form a row, written in one statement. The metadata document of a growing source is an RDF
#   Message Log (version label "1.2-messages"): a Write appends one message, ended by the
#   delimiter MESSAGE. These shapes check the merge of the messages: a SHACL processor that
#   cannot read a message log is given the document without its VERSION line and its
#   delimiters. A missing value has no triple. A source may have no points
#   (yet). The points of a source are the nodes it links to:  <source> tss:hasPoint ?point .
#   A row without a value for a value field has no point for it.
#
#   tss:EmbeddedJSONSource: the rows are JSON. One rdf:JSON literal, tss:points, holds a JSON
#   array with one object per row, keyed by the fields' tss:columnName, e.g.
#     tss:points """[ { "time": "2021-03-03T23:15:00Z", "ec20": "4797.72" } ]"""^^rdf:JSON
#   A value is a JSON string in the lexical form of its field's tss:datatype; "", null or a
#   missing key is no value; "[]" holds no rows. Every field of a tss:EmbeddedJSONSource
#   states its key, tss:columnName (S25). A field of a tss:EmbeddedRDFSource needs no
#   column name, except a describing field that states no tss:property (F13).
#   SHACL does not look inside a literal: these shapes check that tss:points is there and holds
#   a JSON array, but not the rows in it. The point checks (P1-P10, F9, and the times of the
#   points in S23) read the RDF points of a tss:EmbeddedRDFSource.
#
# A tss:ParquetSource, tss:CSVSource or tss:ArrowSource is checked with external_shapes.ttl.
#
# P4 checks the text of each value. rdflib rewrites some texts while it reads Turtle
# (" 12 "^^xsd:double becomes "12.0", "yes"^^xsd:boolean becomes "false"), so P4 sees
# such a wrong text only when the metadata is read with rdflib.NORMALIZE_LITERALS off.
#
# Run:   the dashboard's SHACL tab (code/webapp/backend/main.py),
#        python code/shacl_report/shacl_report.py "<metadata file>.ttl", or
#        pyshacl -s embedded_shapes.ttl "<metadata file>.ttl".
#        The RDF points are part of the metadata, so all three check them.
# The metadata conforms when the report holds no sh:Violation. Warnings point at
# things that look wrong; with -w (allow warnings) they don't fail the run.
#
# A time (tss:from, tss:until, the summary times and the values of the time
# field) is an xsd:dateTime with a timezone (Z or an offset such as +02:00); an
# xsd:dateTimeStamp is allowed too. A time without a timezone does not conform (S23).
#
# The source (tss:EmbeddedJSONSource or tss:EmbeddedRDFSource)
#   Required:  S20 time field datatype (xsd:dateTime or xsd:dateTimeStamp)
#   Required:     S1 the source (one or more embedded sources, each read on its own)
#                 S3 source class: every source states exactly one of the five source classes
#                    (tss:EmbeddedJSONSource, tss:EmbeddedRDFSource, tss:ParquetSource,
#                    tss:CSVSource, tss:ArrowSource)
#                 S24 one kind: every source of the document is embedded (no mixing)
#                 S4 time field  S5 has field (at least one)
#                 S6 points of a tss:EmbeddedRDFSource: every point is a node that exactly
#                    one tss:EmbeddedRDFSource links to with tss:hasPoint, and every node
#                    with a reading of a field of the source is a point of that source
#                 S6 points of a tss:EmbeddedJSONSource: exactly one tss:points, an rdf:JSON
#                    literal that holds a JSON array
#                 S25 JSON keys: every field of a tss:EmbeddedJSONSource states a
#                    tss:columnName, its key in the JSON points
#   Optional:     S2 immutable (true: final; false or not stated: growing, append-only)
#                 S28 range requests (true: while the source grows, its RDF Message Log only
#                    grows, byte for byte, so a consumer fetches only the new messages with
#                    HTTP Range requests); only on a tss:EmbeddedRDFSource, not on a
#                    tss:EmbeddedJSONSource, whose tss:points is rewritten on every Write
#                 S7 label    S8 produced by
#                 S9 key: at most one tss:key, and it is the time field (the key is always the
#                    time field, also when tss:key is not stated)
#                 S10 from    S11 until (after from)
#   Not allowed:  S12 tss:dataFile, tss:delimiter, tss:encoding, tss:header: they describe an
#                 external data file;
#                 tss:timeBase, tss:timeStep, tss:stepField: a time grid is only for an
#                 external data file, so every point states its own time (P1);
#                 tss:points on a tss:EmbeddedRDFSource, and tss:hasPoint on a
#                 tss:EmbeddedJSONSource: each class writes its points in one way
#                 S26 summary of a growing source: only a field of a source that states
#                 tss:immutable true has a tss:summary
#   Warning:      S29 value field: the source has at least one tss:ValueField
#   Required:     S23 timezone: every time has a timezone, also as an xsd:dateTime
#
# The fields (every object of tss:hasField, and every tss:Field, tss:ValueField or
# tss:ContextField): the same checks as in external_shapes.ttl, except F2: a column name is
# optional here
#   Required:  F1 the field: exactly one of tss:ValueField (its values are readings) and
#                 tss:ContextField (its values give the context of a row: the time, the step,
#                 a describing field, an identifier), and a field of exactly one source
#              F3 datatype
#              F11 field kind: the time field and every describing field are context fields
#              F12 context field: a context field states no tss:observedProperty, tss:sensor,
#                  tss:featureOfInterest or tss:aboutUrl
#              F15 describes field: a describing field describes a value field of its source
#   Optional:  F2 column name (unique within the source; required for a field of a
#                 tss:EmbeddedJSONSource, see S25; a field of a tss:EmbeddedRDFSource
#                 needs none, except a describing field without tss:property)
#              F4 column index (unique within the source)   F5 label   F6 comment
#              F7 minimum   F8 maximum (not below the minimum)
#              F10 summary (each summary attribute is also optional)
#              F13 field property: one IRI, only on a describing field, not rdf:type or a TSS
#                  term, unique within the source; a describing field of a
#                  tss:EmbeddedRDFSource states tss:property or tss:columnName
#   Not allowed: F14 tss:aboutUrl on a field of a tss:EmbeddedRDFSource (its points are nodes)
#   Warning:   F9 some point is a reading of the value field (the RDF points)
#
# The value encoding of a field
#   Not allowed:  D3 tss:valueEncoding and tss:baseline: a value encoding is only for an
#                    external data file, so every point states the readings themselves
#
# The points of a tss:EmbeddedRDFSource (the nodes that it links to with tss:hasPoint)
#   Required:  P8 field: every point states its value field (tss:field), a value field of its
#                 source; a point of a source with exactly one value field may leave it out
#              P1 time: every point states its time (tss:time)
#              P9 value: every point states its reading (tss:value)
#              P2 time window: every time is from tss:from (included) until tss:until (not included)
#              P3 key: no two points have the same value field and the same time (the key is
#                 the time field); the same moment written in two ways counts as the same
#              P10 describing: the value of a describing field is only on the points of the
#                  value fields it describes
#              P4 datatype: every value (tss:time, tss:value, and the values of describing
#                 fields) is a literal with its field's tss:datatype,
#                 and a valid value of it (xsd:dateTime, xsd:dateTimeStamp (with a timezone),
#                 xsd:date, xsd:double, xsd:float, xsd:decimal, the integer types and
#                 xsd:boolean are checked); an empty text ("") is no value, so it is not checked
#              P7 one value: a point has one tss:field, one tss:time, one tss:value, and at most
#                 one value for each describing field
#   Warning:   P5 range: a reading outside its field's tss:minimum or tss:maximum (the range is
#                 informative: the value is still valid)
#              P6 properties: every property of a point is tss:field, tss:time, tss:value or
#                 the property of a describing field of its source (so a point states no rdf:type)
# An empty text ("") is no value: P1, P3, P4, P7, F9 and S23 read it as a missing value.
#
# The summary (optional tss:summary on a field of an immutable source; a field of a growing
# source has none, S26): it covers the source's time window
#   Not allowed: Q1 from, Q2 until: a summary has no window of its own
#   Optional:  Q3 missing-value policy   Q4 count   Q5 missing
#              Q6 first time   Q7 last time   Q8 observed minimum   Q9 observed maximum
#              Q10 mean   Q11 median   Q12 generated at time
# An absent summary or an empty summary node is valid. Each supplied attribute
# has at most one value of the stated type. These shapes do not recompute statistics
# or compare observed extrema with the expected tss:minimum / tss:maximum range.
#
# Any other property of a field (tss:observedProperty, tss:unit, tss:sensor, tss:featureOfInterest,
# tss:language, ...) is allowed and not checked.
#
# Every check is in one of these groups (sh:group):
#   Required     sh:Violation  missing or malformed: the metadata does not conform
#   Optional     -             may be left out; when present it must be well-formed (sh:Violation)
#   Not allowed  sh:Violation  contradicts embedded data: the metadata does not conform
#   Warning      sh:Warning    looks wrong, but the metadata still conforms
# (The SPARQL checks have no group: their id says where they belong.)
# =============================================================================

<https://w3id.org/tss/shapes/embedded>
    a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "TSS conformance shapes: readings embedded in the metadata"@en ;
    sh:declare
        [ sh:prefix "tss" ; sh:namespace "https://w3id.org/tss#"^^xsd:anyURI ] ,
        [ sh:prefix "xsd" ; sh:namespace "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#"^^xsd:anyURI ] .


# --- The groups ---------------------------------------------------------------

emb:Required a sh:PropertyGroup ;
    rdfs:label "Required"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Must be present and well-formed (sh:Violation)."@en ;
    sh:order 0 .

emb:Optional a sh:PropertyGroup ;
    rdfs:label "Optional"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "May be left out; when present it must be well-formed (sh:Violation)."@en ;
    sh:order 1 .

emb:NotAllowed a sh:PropertyGroup ;
    rdfs:label "Not allowed"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Contradicts embedded data (sh:Violation)."@en ;
    sh:order 2 .

emb:Warning a sh:PropertyGroup ;
    rdfs:label "Warning"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Looks wrong, but the metadata still conforms (sh:Warning)."@en ;
    sh:order 3 .


# --- S1 the source ------------------------------------------------------------
# sh:targetNode makes tss:Source the focus node, so this check also runs (and fails)
# when the metadata holds no embedded source at all.

emb:SourceExistsShape a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetNode tss:Source ;
    sh:sparql [
        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;
        sh:message "S1 the source: the metadata must describe at least one embedded source, a tss:EmbeddedJSONSource or a tss:EmbeddedRDFSource; each source is read on its own. A tss:ParquetSource, tss:CSVSource or tss:ArrowSource is checked with external_shapes.ttl." ;
        sh:prefixes <https://w3id.org/tss/shapes/embedded> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT $this WHERE {
                FILTER NOT EXISTS {
                    ?source a ?class .
                    FILTER (?class IN (tss:EmbeddedJSONSource, tss:EmbeddedRDFSource))
                }
            }""" ;
    ] .


# --- The source ---------------------------------------------------------------

emb:SourceShape a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetClass tss:EmbeddedJSONSource, tss:EmbeddedRDFSource ;

    # Required
    sh:property [
        sh:name "S2 immutable" ;
        sh:group emb:Optional ;
        sh:path tss:immutable ;
        sh:maxCount 1 ;
        sh:datatype xsd:boolean ;
        sh:message "tss:immutable must be one xsd:boolean: true (final: no point is added, changed or removed) or false (growing: points may be added, but none is changed or removed). Not stated means false." ;
    ] ;
    sh:property [
        sh:name "S28 range requests" ;
        sh:group emb:Optional ;
        sh:path tss:rangeRequests ;
        sh:maxCount 1 ;
        sh:datatype xsd:boolean ;
        sh:message "tss:rangeRequests must be one xsd:boolean: true (while the source grows, its RDF Message Log only grows, byte for byte, so a consumer may fetch only the new messages with HTTP Range requests) or false (the document may be written anew on every change). Not stated means false." ;
    ] ;
    sh:property [
        sh:name "S4 time field" ;
        sh:group emb:Required ;
        sh:path tss:timeField ;
        sh:minCount 1 ;
        sh:maxCount 1 ;
        sh:nodeKind sh:BlankNodeOrIRI ;
        sh:message "The source needs exactly one tss:timeField: the field that holds the time of each row." ;
    ] ;
    sh:property [
        sh:name "S5 has field" ;
        sh:group emb:Required ;
        sh:path tss:hasField ;
        sh:minCount 1 ;
        sh:nodeKind sh:BlankNodeOrIRI ;
        sh:message "The source needs at least one tss:hasField, and each of them must be a field node: a tss:ValueField or a tss:ContextField (F1)." ;
    ] ;

    # Optional
    sh:property [
        sh:name "S7 label" ;
        sh:group emb:Optional ;
        sh:path rdfs:label ;
        sh:nodeKind sh:Literal ;
        sh:message "rdfs:label must be a text." ;
    ] ;
    sh:property [
        sh:name "S8 produced by" ;
        sh:group emb:Optional ;
        sh:path tss:producedBy ;
        sh:maxCount 1 ;
        sh:nodeKind sh:IRI ;
        sh:message "tss:producedBy must be one IRI (the station or system that produced the data)." ;
    ] ;
    sh:property [
        sh:name "S9 key" ;
        sh:group emb:Optional ;
        sh:path tss:key ;
        sh:maxCount 1 ;
        sh:nodeKind sh:BlankNodeOrIRI ;
        sh:message "tss:key must be one field, the time field: its values identify a point. A source without tss:key has its time field as key." ;
    ] ;
    sh:property [
        sh:name "S10 from" ;
        sh:group emb:Optional ;
        sh:path tss:from ;
        sh:maxCount 1 ;
        sh:or ( [ sh:datatype xsd:dateTime ] [ sh:datatype xsd:dateTimeStamp ] ) ;
        sh:message "tss:from must be one xsd:dateTime (with a timezone): the start of the time window." ;
    ] ;
    sh:property [
        sh:name "S11 until" ;
        sh:group emb:Optional ;
        sh:path tss:until ;
        sh:maxCount 1 ;
        sh:or ( [ sh:datatype xsd:dateTime ] [ sh:datatype xsd:dateTimeStamp ] ) ;
        sh:message "tss:until must be one xsd:dateTime (with a timezone): the end of the time window (not included)." ;
    ] ;
    # Not allowed: these describe an external data file
    sh:property [
        sh:name "S12 data file" ;
        sh:group emb:NotAllowed ;
        sh:path tss:dataFile ;
        sh:maxCount 0 ;
        sh:message "S12 not allowed: an embedded source keeps its points in the metadata itself, so it has no tss:dataFile." ;
    ] ;
    sh:property [
        sh:name "S12 delimiter" ;
        sh:group emb:NotAllowed ;
        sh:path tss:delimiter ;
        sh:maxCount 0 ;
        sh:message "S12 not allowed: tss:delimiter describes a CSV data file, not embedded points." ;
    ] ;
    sh:property [
        sh:name "S12 encoding" ;
        sh:group emb:NotAllowed ;
        sh:path tss:encoding ;
        sh:maxCount 0 ;
        sh:message "S12 not allowed: tss:encoding describes a CSV data file, not embedded points." ;
    ] ;
    sh:property [
        sh:name "S12 header" ;
        sh:group emb:NotAllowed ;
        sh:path tss:header ;
        sh:maxCount 0 ;
        sh:message "S12 not allowed: tss:header describes a CSV data file, not embedded points." ;
    ] ;
    # Not allowed: a time grid is only for an external data file; every point states its own time (P1)
    sh:property [
        sh:name "S12 time base" ;
        sh:group emb:NotAllowed ;
        sh:path tss:timeBase ;
        sh:maxCount 0 ;
        sh:message "S12 not allowed: tss:timeBase is part of a time grid, which is only for a source with an external data file; every embedded point states its own time." ;
    ] ;
    sh:property [
        sh:name "S12 time step" ;
        sh:group emb:NotAllowed ;
        sh:path tss:timeStep ;
        sh:maxCount 0 ;
        sh:message "S12 not allowed: tss:timeStep is part of a time grid, which is only for a source with an external data file; every embedded point states its own time." ;
    ] ;
    sh:property [
        sh:name "S12 step field" ;
        sh:group emb:NotAllowed ;
        sh:path tss:stepField ;
        sh:maxCount 0 ;
        sh:message "S12 not allowed: tss:stepField names the step column of a data file; every embedded point states its own time." ;
    ] ;

    # S4: the time field is a field of this source; S9: the key is the time field
    sh:sparql [
        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;
        sh:message "S4 time field: tss:timeField must be one of the source's own fields (tss:hasField)." ;
        sh:prefixes <https://w3id.org/tss/shapes/embedded> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT $this ?value WHERE {
                $this tss:timeField ?value .
                FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this tss:hasField ?value }
            }""" ;
    ] ;
    sh:sparql [
        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;
        sh:message "S9 key: tss:key is {?value}, but the key of a source is its time field (tss:timeField): no two points have the same time." ;
        sh:prefixes <https://w3id.org/tss/shapes/embedded> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT $this ?value WHERE {
                $this tss:key ?value .
                FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this tss:timeField ?value }
            }""" ;
    ] ;

    # S20: the time field's values are times of the source, and every time of a source is an
    # xsd:dateTime with a timezone (xsd:dateTimeStamp is allowed too)
    sh:sparql [
        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;
        sh:message "S20 time field datatype: the time field's tss:datatype is {?value}, but every time of a source is an xsd:dateTime (with a timezone), or an xsd:dateTimeStamp." ;
        sh:prefixes <https://w3id.org/tss/shapes/embedded> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT $this ?value WHERE {
                $this tss:timeField ?timeField .
                ?timeField tss:datatype ?value .
                FILTER (!sameTerm(?value, xsd:dateTime) && !sameTerm(?value, xsd:dateTimeStamp))
            }""" ;
    ] ;

    # S11: the time window is not empty
    sh:sparql [
        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;
        sh:message "S11 until: tss:until must come after tss:from." ;
        sh:prefixes <https://w3id.org/tss/shapes/embedded> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT $this ?value WHERE {
                $this tss:from ?from ; tss:until ?value .
                # The moments (S23 reports a time without a timezone; here it is read as UTC)
                BIND (xsd:dateTime(IF(REGEX(STR(?from), "(Z|[+-][0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2})$"), STR(?from), CONCAT(STR(?from), "Z"))) AS ?start)
                BIND (xsd:dateTime(IF(REGEX(STR(?value), "(Z|[+-][0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2})$"), STR(?value), CONCAT(STR(?value), "Z"))) AS ?end)
                FILTER (BOUND(?start) && BOUND(?end) && ?end <= ?start)
            }""" ;
    ] .


# --- S3: the source class ------------------------------------------------------------
# Every source, that is every node with a tss:hasField and every node typed tss:Source or one
# of its five classes, states exactly one of the five source classes: the class says where its
# points are and how to read them.

emb:SourceClassShape a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetSubjectsOf tss:hasField ;
    sh:targetClass tss:Source, tss:EmbeddedJSONSource, tss:EmbeddedRDFSource,
        tss:ParquetSource, tss:CSVSource, tss:ArrowSource ;
    sh:sparql [
        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;
        sh:message "S3 source class: the source states none of the five source classes (tss:EmbeddedJSONSource, tss:EmbeddedRDFSource, tss:ParquetSource, tss:CSVSource, tss:ArrowSource), so nothing says where its points are." ;
        sh:prefixes <https://w3id.org/tss/shapes/embedded> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT $this WHERE {
                FILTER NOT EXISTS {
                    $this a ?class .
                    FILTER (?class IN (tss:EmbeddedJSONSource, tss:EmbeddedRDFSource, tss:ParquetSource, tss:CSVSource, tss:ArrowSource))
                }
            }""" ;
    ] ;
    sh:sparql [
        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;
        sh:message "S3 source class: the source states two source classes, {?value} and {?other}; a source states exactly one." ;
        sh:prefixes <https://w3id.org/tss/shapes/embedded> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT DISTINCT $this ?value ?other WHERE {
                $this a ?value, ?other .
                FILTER (?value IN (tss:EmbeddedJSONSource, tss:EmbeddedRDFSource, tss:ParquetSource, tss:CSVSource, tss:ArrowSource))
                FILTER (?other IN (tss:EmbeddedJSONSource, tss:EmbeddedRDFSource, tss:ParquetSource, tss:CSVSource, tss:ArrowSource))
                FILTER (STR(?value) < STR(?other))
            }""" ;
    ] .


# --- S24: one kind of source per document --------------------------------------
# A document describes embedded sources or external sources, never both, so that one set
# of rules (and one shapes file) reads all of its sources.

emb:OneKindShape a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetClass tss:EmbeddedJSONSource, tss:EmbeddedRDFSource ;
    sh:sparql [
        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;
        sh:message "S24 one kind: the document also describes the external source {?value}; all sources of a document are embedded, or all are external, never both." ;
        sh:prefixes <https://w3id.org/tss/shapes/embedded> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT DISTINCT $this ?value WHERE {
                ?value a ?class .
                FILTER (?class IN (tss:ParquetSource, tss:CSVSource, tss:ArrowSource))
            }""" ;
    ] .


# --- S23: every time has a timezone ----------------------------------------------
# Every time is an xsd:dateTime (or xsd:dateTimeStamp) with a timezone: a time without one
# does not conform, also when its datatype is xsd:dateTime, which allows one to be left out. (The sh:datatype checks only compare the datatype IRI; S23 reads the text.)

emb:TimezoneShape a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetClass tss:EmbeddedJSONSource, tss:EmbeddedRDFSource ;
    sh:sparql [
        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;
        sh:message "S23 timezone: {?value} ({?where}) has no timezone. Every time MUST have a timezone, such as Z or +02:00, also as an xsd:dateTime." ;
        sh:prefixes <https://w3id.org/tss/shapes/embedded> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT DISTINCT $this ?value ?where WHERE {
                {
                    # A time of the source
                    $this ?property ?value .
                    FILTER (?property IN (tss:from, tss:until, tss:timeBase))
                    BIND (CONCAT("the source's ", REPLACE(STR(?property), "^.*#", "tss:")) AS ?where)
                } UNION {
                    # A time of a summary
                    $this tss:hasField ?field .
                    ?field tss:summary ?summary .
                    ?summary ?property ?value .
                    FILTER (?property IN (tss:firstTime, tss:lastTime, tss:generatedAtTime))
                    BIND (CONCAT("a summary's ", REPLACE(STR(?property), "^.*#", "tss:")) AS ?where)
                } UNION {
                    # The time of a point
                    $this tss:hasPoint ?point .
                    ?point tss:time ?value .
                    BIND ("the time of a point" AS ?where)
                }
                FILTER (isLiteral(?value) && STR(?value) != "" && !REGEX(STR(?value), "(Z|[+-][0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2})$"))
            }""" ;
    ] .


# --- S6 and S12: how the points are written ---------------------------------------
# A tss:EmbeddedJSONSource writes its points as JSON, in one tss:points literal; a
# tss:EmbeddedRDFSource writes them as RDF nodes that it links to with tss:hasPoint.
# SHACL does not look inside the JSON: S6 only checks that it holds an array.

emb:JSONSourceShape a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetClass tss:EmbeddedJSONSource ;
    # S28: a Write rewrites tss:points, so the bytes of the document do not only grow
    sh:sparql [
        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;
        sh:message "S28 range requests: a tss:EmbeddedJSONSource cannot state tss:rangeRequests true; a Write rewrites its tss:points, so the earlier bytes of its document change." ;
        sh:prefixes <https://w3id.org/tss/shapes/embedded> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT $this ?value WHERE {
                $this tss:rangeRequests ?value .
                FILTER (?value = true)
            }""" ;
    ] ;
    sh:property [
        sh:name "S6 points" ;
        sh:group emb:Required ;
        sh:path tss:points ;
        sh:minCount 1 ;
        sh:maxCount 1 ;
        sh:datatype rdf:JSON ;
        sh:message "A tss:EmbeddedJSONSource needs exactly one tss:points: an rdf:JSON literal with its points, a JSON array of objects." ;
    ] ;
    sh:property [
        sh:name "S6 points hold a JSON array" ;
        sh:group emb:Required ;
        sh:path tss:points ;
        # [\s\S] is any character, also a line break (no sh:flags "s": not every engine has it)
        sh:pattern "^\\s*\\[[\\s\\S]*\\]\\s*$" ;
        sh:message "tss:points must hold a JSON array of objects, one per point, such as [ { \"time\": \"2021-03-03T23:15:00Z\", \"ec20\": \"4797.72\" } ]; \"[]\" holds no points." ;
    ] ;
    sh:property [
        sh:name "S25 JSON keys" ;
        sh:group emb:Required ;
        sh:path tss:hasField ;
        sh:node emb:JSONKeyShape ;
        sh:message "S25: every field of a tss:EmbeddedJSONSource needs a tss:columnName, its key in the JSON points." ;
    ] ;
    sh:property [
        sh:name "S12 has point" ;
        sh:group emb:NotAllowed ;
        sh:path tss:hasPoint ;
        sh:maxCount 0 ;
        sh:message "S12 not allowed: the points of a tss:EmbeddedJSONSource are the objects in its tss:points; tss:hasPoint links the RDF points of a tss:EmbeddedRDFSource." ;
    ] .

# S25: a field of a tss:EmbeddedJSONSource has a column name (F2 checks its form)
emb:JSONKeyShape a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:property [
        sh:path tss:columnName ;
        sh:minCount 1 ;
        sh:message "S25: a field of a tss:EmbeddedJSONSource needs a tss:columnName, its key in the JSON points." ;
    ] .

emb:RDFSourceShape a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetClass tss:EmbeddedRDFSource ;
    sh:property [
        sh:name "S12 points" ;
        sh:group emb:NotAllowed ;
        sh:path tss:points ;
        sh:maxCount 0 ;
        sh:message "S12 not allowed: the points of a tss:EmbeddedRDFSource are the RDF nodes it links to with tss:hasPoint; tss:points holds the JSON points of a tss:EmbeddedJSONSource." ;
    ] .


# --- The fields ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Every tss:Field, and every object of tss:hasField (so an untyped field is checked too)

emb:FieldShape a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetClass tss:Field, tss:ValueField, tss:ContextField ;
    sh:targetObjectsOf tss:hasField ;

    # Required
    sh:property [
        sh:name "F1 the field belongs to a source" ;
        sh:group emb:Required ;
        sh:path [ sh:inversePath tss:hasField ] ;
        sh:minCount 1 ;
        sh:maxCount 1 ;
        sh:message "A field must be a field (tss:hasField) of exactly one source." ;
    ] ;
    sh:property [
        sh:name "F3 datatype" ;
        sh:group emb:Required ;
        sh:path tss:datatype ;
        sh:minCount 1 ;
        sh:maxCount 1 ;
        sh:nodeKind sh:IRI ;
        sh:message "A field needs exactly one tss:datatype, an IRI such as xsd:double or xsd:dateTime." ;
    ] ;

    # Optional
    # F2: a field of a tss:EmbeddedJSONSource must state its column name (S25)
    sh:property [
        sh:name "F2 column name" ;
        sh:group emb:Optional ;
        sh:path tss:columnName ;
        sh:maxCount 1 ;
        sh:datatype xsd:string ;
        sh:minLength 1 ;
        sh:message "tss:columnName must be one non-empty text: the field's key in the JSON rows. A field of a tss:EmbeddedRDFSource needs none, except a describing field that states no tss:property." ;
    ] ;
    sh:property [
        sh:name "F4 column index" ;
        sh:group emb:Optional ;
        sh:path tss:columnIndex ;
        sh:maxCount 1 ;
        sh:datatype xsd:integer ;
        sh:minInclusive 0 ;
        sh:message "tss:columnIndex must be one whole number, 0 or more (the first column is 0)." ;
    ] ;
    sh:property [
        sh:name "F5 label" ;
        sh:group emb:Optional ;
        sh:path rdfs:label ;
        sh:nodeKind sh:Literal ;
        sh:message "rdfs:label must be a text." ;
    ] ;
    sh:property [
        sh:name "F6 comment" ;
        sh:group emb:Optional ;
        sh:path rdfs:comment ;
        sh:nodeKind sh:Literal ;
        sh:message "rdfs:comment must be a text." ;
    ] ;
    sh:property [
        sh:name "F7 minimum" ;
        sh:group emb:Optional ;
        sh:path tss:minimum ;
        sh:maxCount 1 ;
        sh:or ( [ sh:datatype xsd:integer ] [ sh:datatype xsd:decimal ] [ sh:datatype xsd:double ] [ sh:datatype xsd:float ] ) ;
        sh:message "tss:minimum must be one number (xsd:integer, xsd:decimal, xsd:double or xsd:float)." ;
    ] ;
    sh:property [
        sh:name "F8 maximum" ;
        sh:group emb:Optional ;
        sh:path tss:maximum ;
        sh:maxCount 1 ;
        sh:or ( [ sh:datatype xsd:integer ] [ sh:datatype xsd:decimal ] [ sh:datatype xsd:double ] [ sh:datatype xsd:float ] ) ;
        sh:message "tss:maximum must be one number (xsd:integer, xsd:decimal, xsd:double or xsd:float)." ;
    ] ;

    sh:property [
        sh:name "F13 field property" ;
        sh:group emb:Optional ;
        sh:path tss:property ;
        sh:maxCount 1 ;
        sh:nodeKind sh:IRI ;
        sh:message "tss:property must be one IRI: the property that states the values of a describing field on the points it describes." ;
    ] ;
    sh:property [
        sh:name "F14 about URL" ;
        sh:group emb:Optional ;
        sh:path tss:aboutUrl ;
        sh:maxCount 1 ;
        sh:datatype xsd:string ;
        sh:message "tss:aboutUrl must be one text: a URI template (RFC 6570) that makes the IRI of each point of a value field." ;
    ] ;
    sh:property [
        sh:name "F10 summary" ;
        sh:group emb:Optional ;
        sh:path tss:summary ;
        sh:maxCount 1 ;
        sh:nodeKind sh:BlankNodeOrIRI ;
        sh:node emb:SummaryShape ;
        sh:message "tss:summary must point to one summary node; the summary and all its attributes may be omitted." ;
    ] ;

    # Not allowed: a value encoding is only for an external data file; every point states the
    # readings themselves
    sh:property [
        sh:name "D3 value encoding" ;
        sh:group emb:NotAllowed ;
        sh:path tss:valueEncoding ;
        sh:maxCount 0 ;
        sh:message "D3 not allowed: a tss:valueEncoding is only for a field of a source with an external data file; every embedded point states the readings themselves." ;
    ] ;
    sh:property [
        sh:name "D3 baseline" ;
        sh:group emb:NotAllowed ;
        sh:path tss:baseline ;
        sh:maxCount 0 ;
        sh:message "D3 not allowed: a tss:baseline belongs to a value encoding, which is only for a field of a source with an external data file; every embedded point states the readings themselves." ;
    ] ;

    # F2 and F4: two fields of the same source can't use the same key or index
    sh:sparql [
        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;
        sh:message "F2 column name: another field of the same source has the column name {?value}." ;
        sh:prefixes <https://w3id.org/tss/shapes/embedded> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT $this ?value WHERE {
                ?source tss:hasField $this, ?other .
                $this tss:columnName ?value .
                ?other tss:columnName ?value .
                FILTER (?other != $this)
            }""" ;
    ] ;
    sh:sparql [
        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;
        sh:message "F4 column index: another field of the same source has the column index {?value}." ;
        sh:prefixes <https://w3id.org/tss/shapes/embedded> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT $this ?value WHERE {
                ?source tss:hasField $this, ?other .
                $this tss:columnIndex ?value .
                ?other tss:columnIndex ?value .
                FILTER (?other != $this)
            }""" ;
    ] ;

    # F8: the expected range is not empty
    sh:sparql [
        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;
        sh:message "F8 maximum: tss:maximum ({?value}) is below tss:minimum." ;
        sh:prefixes <https://w3id.org/tss/shapes/embedded> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT $this ?value WHERE {
                $this tss:minimum ?minimum ; tss:maximum ?value .
                FILTER (?value < ?minimum)
            }""" ;
    ] ;

    # F1: every field is a value field (its values are readings) or a context field (its
    # values give the context of a row: the time, the step, a describing field, an identifier)
    sh:sparql [
        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;
        sh:message "F1 the field: a field states one of tss:ValueField and tss:ContextField as its rdf:type: whether its values are readings or give the context of a row." ;
        sh:prefixes <https://w3id.org/tss/shapes/embedded> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT $this WHERE {
                FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this a ?kind . FILTER (?kind IN (tss:ValueField, tss:ContextField)) }
            }""" ;
    ] ;
    sh:sparql [
        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;
        sh:message "F1 the field: a field is a tss:ValueField or a tss:ContextField, not both." ;
        sh:prefixes <https://w3id.org/tss/shapes/embedded> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT $this WHERE {
                $this a tss:ValueField, tss:ContextField .
            }""" ;
    ] ;
    # F11: the time field, the step field and every describing field are context fields
    sh:sparql [
        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;
        sh:message "F11 field kind: this field is {?role}, so it is a tss:ContextField, not a tss:ValueField: its values are not readings." ;
        sh:prefixes <https://w3id.org/tss/shapes/embedded> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT DISTINCT $this ?role WHERE {
                $this a tss:ValueField .
                { ?source tss:timeField $this . BIND ("the time field" AS ?role) }
                UNION { ?source tss:stepField $this . BIND ("the step field" AS ?role) }
                UNION { $this tss:describesField ?described . BIND ("a describing field" AS ?role) }
            }""" ;
    ] ;
    # F12: what a reading means is stated on a value field only
    sh:sparql [
        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;
        sh:message "F12 context field: a tss:ContextField states no {?value}: its values are not readings, so they observe nothing." ;
        sh:prefixes <https://w3id.org/tss/shapes/embedded> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT DISTINCT $this ?value WHERE {
                $this a tss:ContextField ; ?value ?any .
                FILTER (?value IN (tss:observedProperty, tss:sensor, tss:featureOfInterest, tss:aboutUrl))
            }""" ;
    ] ;
    # F13: only a describing field states tss:property: the property that states its values on
    # the points it describes. A point states its time and its reading with tss:time and tss:value.
    sh:sparql [
        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;
        sh:message "F13 field property: only a describing field (tss:describesField) states tss:property; a point states its time with tss:time and its reading with tss:value." ;
        sh:prefixes <https://w3id.org/tss/shapes/embedded> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT $this ?value WHERE {
                $this tss:property ?value .
                FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this tss:describesField ?described }
            }""" ;
    ] ;
    sh:sparql [
        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;
        sh:message "F13 field property: tss:property is {?value}, which is rdf:type or a term of the TSS vocabulary; a describing field states its values with a property of its own." ;
        sh:prefixes <https://w3id.org/tss/shapes/embedded> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT $this ?value WHERE {
                $this tss:property ?value .
                FILTER (?value = <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> || STRSTARTS(STR(?value), "https://w3id.org/tss#"))
            }""" ;
    ] ;
    sh:sparql [
        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;
        sh:message "F13 field property: another describing field of the same source has the property {?value}." ;
        sh:prefixes <https://w3id.org/tss/shapes/embedded> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT $this ?value WHERE {
                ?source tss:hasField $this, ?other .
                $this tss:property ?value .
                ?other tss:property ?value .
                FILTER (?other != $this)
            }""" ;
    ] ;
    # F15: a describing field describes a value field of its own source
    sh:sparql [
        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;
        sh:message "F15 describes field: {?value} is not a value field (tss:ValueField) of the same source; a describing field says something about the readings of a value field in the same row." ;
        sh:prefixes <https://w3id.org/tss/shapes/embedded> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT $this ?value WHERE {
                $this tss:describesField ?value .
                FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?source tss:hasField $this, ?value . ?value a tss:ValueField }
            }""" ;
    ] ;
    # F13: a describing field of a tss:EmbeddedRDFSource has no default property unless it
    # states a column name, so it states tss:property or tss:columnName
    # F14: the points of a tss:EmbeddedRDFSource are RDF nodes already: no tss:aboutUrl
    sh:sparql [
        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;
        sh:message "F13 field property: a describing field of a tss:EmbeddedRDFSource states tss:property, or a tss:columnName that its default property is made from." ;
        sh:prefixes <https://w3id.org/tss/shapes/embedded> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT $this WHERE {
                ?source a tss:EmbeddedRDFSource ; tss:hasField $this .
                $this tss:describesField ?described .
                FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this tss:property ?property }
                FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this tss:columnName ?name }
            }""" ;
    ] ;
    sh:sparql [
        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;
        sh:message "F14 about URL: a field of a tss:EmbeddedRDFSource states no tss:aboutUrl; its points are RDF nodes already, blank nodes or IRIs." ;
        sh:prefixes <https://w3id.org/tss/shapes/embedded> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT $this ?value WHERE {
                ?source a tss:EmbeddedRDFSource ; tss:hasField $this .
                $this tss:aboutUrl ?value .
            }""" ;
    ] ; .


# --- F9: some point is a reading of the value field -----------------------------
# A shape of its own, because a SPARQL check takes its severity from its shape.
# The points of a value field are the points that state it with tss:field, or, when the source
# has one value field, the points that state no tss:field. Only when the source has points at
# all: a source without points (yet) gives no warning per field.

emb:FieldInPointsShape a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetClass tss:Field, tss:ValueField, tss:ContextField ;
    sh:targetObjectsOf tss:hasField ;
    sh:severity sh:Warning ;
    sh:sparql [
        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;
        sh:message "F9 points: the source has points, but none is a reading of this value field, so it has no values." ;
        sh:prefixes <https://w3id.org/tss/shapes/embedded> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT $this WHERE {
                ?source tss:hasField $this .
                $this a tss:ValueField .
                FILTER EXISTS { ?source tss:hasPoint ?anyPoint }
                FILTER NOT EXISTS {
                    ?source tss:hasPoint ?point .
                    { ?point tss:field $this } UNION { FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?point tss:field ?anyField1 } ?source tss:hasField $this . $this a tss:ValueField . FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?source tss:hasField ?otherField1 . ?otherField1 a tss:ValueField . FILTER (?otherField1 != $this) } }
                }
            }""" ;
    ] .


# --- S6: the points and their source ---------------------------------------------
# A point is a node that a source links to with tss:hasPoint: a blank node or an IRI,
# not a literal, since its values are triples about it. It is a point of exactly one source.

emb:PointShape a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetObjectsOf tss:hasPoint ;
    sh:nodeKind sh:BlankNodeOrIRI ;
    sh:message "S6 points: a point is a node (a blank node or an IRI) that holds its values, not a literal." ;
    sh:property [
        sh:name "S6 has point" ;
        sh:group emb:Required ;
        sh:path [ sh:inversePath tss:hasPoint ] ;
        sh:maxCount 1 ;
        sh:class tss:EmbeddedRDFSource ;
        sh:message "S6 points: a point is a point of exactly one tss:EmbeddedRDFSource: one source links to it with tss:hasPoint." ;
    ] .


# --- The points: S6, P1-P3 and P7-P10, about each point --------------------------
# The points of the source are the nodes it links to:   $this tss:hasPoint ?point .
# A point states its value field (tss:field), its time (tss:time) and its reading (tss:value),
# and the values of the describing fields that describe its value field, each with the
# tss:property of that describing field. A point of a source with one value field may leave
# out tss:field. sh:value is the point, so the report shows its values.

emb:PointsShape a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetClass tss:EmbeddedRDFSource ;

    # S6: a reading of one of the source's fields is in a point of the source. A node that
    # states a field of this source with tss:field, but that the source does not link to with
    # tss:hasPoint (left out, or a typo in the source's IRI), is not one of its points; nor is
    # a node with a tss:time or tss:value that no source links to.
    sh:sparql [
        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;
        sh:message "S6 points: a node has a reading or a time, but the source does not link to it with tss:hasPoint, so it is not one of its points." ;
        sh:prefixes <https://w3id.org/tss/shapes/embedded> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT DISTINCT $this ?value WHERE {
                {
                    $this tss:hasField ?field .
                    ?value tss:field ?field .
                    FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this tss:hasPoint ?value }
                } UNION {
                    ?value tss:time|tss:value ?any .
                    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?value tss:field ?field }
                    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?anySource tss:hasPoint ?value }
                }
            }""" ;
    ] ;

    # P8: a point states its value field, unless its source has exactly one value field
    sh:sparql [
        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;
        sh:message "P8 field: a point states no tss:field, but its source does not have exactly one value field, so nothing says which field its reading belongs to." ;
        sh:prefixes <https://w3id.org/tss/shapes/embedded> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT DISTINCT $this ?value WHERE {
                $this tss:hasPoint ?value .
                FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?value tss:field ?field }
                FILTER NOT EXISTS {
                    $this tss:hasField ?only . ?only a tss:ValueField .
                    FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this tss:hasField ?other . ?other a tss:ValueField . FILTER (?other != ?only) }
                }
            }""" ;
    ] ;
    sh:sparql [
        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;
        sh:message "P8 field: a point states tss:field {?field}, which is not a value field (tss:ValueField) of its source." ;
        sh:prefixes <https://w3id.org/tss/shapes/embedded> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT DISTINCT $this ?value ?field WHERE {
                $this tss:hasPoint ?value .
                ?value tss:field ?field .
                FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this tss:hasField ?field . ?field a tss:ValueField }
            }""" ;
    ] ;

    # P1: every point has a time (tss:time)
    sh:sparql [
        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;
        sh:message "P1 time: a point has no time: no tss:time." ;
        sh:prefixes <https://w3id.org/tss/shapes/embedded> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT DISTINCT $this ?value WHERE {
                $this tss:hasPoint ?value .
                FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?value tss:time ?time . FILTER (STR(?time) != "") }
            }""" ;
    ] ;

    # P9: every point has a reading (tss:value): a row without a value for a value field has
    # no point for it
    sh:sparql [
        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;
        sh:message "P9 value: a point has no reading: no tss:value." ;
        sh:prefixes <https://w3id.org/tss/shapes/embedded> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT DISTINCT $this ?value WHERE {
                $this tss:hasPoint ?value .
                FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?value tss:value ?reading . FILTER (STR(?reading) != "") }
            }""" ;
    ] ;

    # P2: every time is inside the window [tss:from, tss:until).
    # xsd:dateTime(...) gives no value for a time that is not a valid date-time;
    # P4 reports those, so they are skipped here. A time without a timezone (of a point, or
    # tss:from / tss:until) does not conform (S23, P4); here it is read as UTC so the window is
    # still checked: it gets a "Z" before it is compared.
    sh:sparql [
        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;
        sh:message "P2 time window: the point at {?value} is before tss:from." ;
        sh:prefixes <https://w3id.org/tss/shapes/embedded> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT $this ?value WHERE {
                $this tss:from ?from ; tss:hasPoint ?point .
                ?point tss:time ?value .
                BIND (xsd:dateTime(IF(REGEX(STR(?value), "(Z|[+-][0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2})$"), STR(?value), CONCAT(STR(?value), "Z"))) AS ?moment)
                BIND (xsd:dateTime(IF(REGEX(STR(?from), "(Z|[+-][0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2})$"), STR(?from), CONCAT(STR(?from), "Z"))) AS ?bound)
                FILTER (BOUND(?moment) && BOUND(?bound) && ?moment < ?bound)
            }""" ;
    ] ;
    sh:sparql [
        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;
        sh:message "P2 time window: the point at {?value} is not before tss:until (until is not included)." ;
        sh:prefixes <https://w3id.org/tss/shapes/embedded> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT $this ?value WHERE {
                $this tss:until ?until ; tss:hasPoint ?point .
                ?point tss:time ?value .
                BIND (xsd:dateTime(IF(REGEX(STR(?value), "(Z|[+-][0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2})$"), STR(?value), CONCAT(STR(?value), "Z"))) AS ?moment)
                BIND (xsd:dateTime(IF(REGEX(STR(?until), "(Z|[+-][0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2})$"), STR(?until), CONCAT(STR(?until), "Z"))) AS ?bound)
                FILTER (BOUND(?moment) && BOUND(?bound) && ?moment >= ?bound)
            }""" ;
    ] ;

    # P3: the key identifies a row, so no two points of a source have the same value field and
    # the same time. The same moment written in two ways (2021-03-03T23:15:00Z and
    # 2021-03-03T23:15:00+00:00, or 2021-03-03T23:15:00 without a timezone, which S23 reports and
    # which is read as UTC here) is the same time too.
    sh:sparql [
        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;
        sh:message "P3 key: more than one point of the value field {?field} has the time {?value}." ;
        sh:prefixes <https://w3id.org/tss/shapes/embedded> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT DISTINCT $this ?value ?field WHERE {
                $this tss:hasPoint ?point, ?other .
                FILTER (?other != ?point)
                ?point tss:time ?value .
                ?other tss:time ?otherTime .
                FILTER (isLiteral(?value) && STR(?value) != "")
                { ?point tss:field ?field } UNION { FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?point tss:field ?anyField1 } $this tss:hasField ?field . ?field a tss:ValueField . FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this tss:hasField ?otherField1 . ?otherField1 a tss:ValueField . FILTER (?otherField1 != ?field) } }
                { ?other tss:field ?field } UNION { FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?other tss:field ?anyField2 } $this tss:hasField ?field . ?field a tss:ValueField . FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this tss:hasField ?otherField2 . ?otherField2 a tss:ValueField . FILTER (?otherField2 != ?field) } }
                BIND (xsd:dateTime(IF(REGEX(STR(?value), "(Z|[+-][0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2})$"), STR(?value), CONCAT(STR(?value), "Z"))) AS ?moment)
                BIND (xsd:dateTime(IF(REGEX(STR(?otherTime), "(Z|[+-][0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2})$"), STR(?otherTime), CONCAT(STR(?otherTime), "Z"))) AS ?otherMoment)
                # The same text, or (for valid times) the same moment
                FILTER (sameTerm(?value, ?otherTime)
                    || (BOUND(?moment) && BOUND(?otherMoment) && ?moment = ?otherMoment))
            }""" ;
    ] ;

    # P7: a point has one value field, one time, one reading, and at most one value for each
    # describing field
    sh:sparql [
        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;
        sh:message "P7 one value: a point has more than one value for {?property}." ;
        sh:prefixes <https://w3id.org/tss/shapes/embedded> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT DISTINCT $this ?value ?property WHERE {
                $this tss:hasPoint ?value .
                ?value ?property ?first, ?second .
                FILTER (!sameTerm(?first, ?second))
                FILTER (?property IN (tss:field, tss:time, tss:value)
                    || EXISTS { $this tss:hasField ?describing . ?describing tss:property ?property })
                # An empty text is no value
                FILTER ((!isLiteral(?first) || STR(?first) != "") && (!isLiteral(?second) || STR(?second) != ""))
            }""" ;
    ] ;

    # P10: the value of a describing field is stated on the points of the fields it describes,
    # and on no other point
    sh:sparql [
        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;
        sh:message "P10 describing: a point states {?property}, the property of the describing field {?describing}, which does not describe the value field of the point." ;
        sh:prefixes <https://w3id.org/tss/shapes/embedded> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT DISTINCT $this ?value ?property ?describing WHERE {
                $this tss:hasField ?describing .
                ?describing tss:property ?property .
                $this tss:hasPoint ?value .
                ?value ?property ?any .
                { ?value tss:field ?field } UNION { FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?value tss:field ?anyField1 } $this tss:hasField ?field . ?field a tss:ValueField . FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this tss:hasField ?otherField1 . ?otherField1 a tss:ValueField . FILTER (?otherField1 != ?field) } }
                FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?describing tss:describesField ?field }
            }""" ;
    ] .


# --- The points: P4, about the values of one field -------------------------
# The focus node is the field; sh:value is the value that is wrong.
# ?when is the time of the point, to find it among the points.
# The values of a field on the points: for the time field, tss:time; for a value field,
# tss:value of its points; for a describing field, its tss:property.

emb:FieldValuesShape a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetClass tss:Field, tss:ValueField, tss:ContextField ;
    sh:targetObjectsOf tss:hasField ;

    # P4: the value is a literal with the field's datatype (not a literal of another
    # datatype, a text with a language tag, or an IRI or blank node)
    sh:sparql [
        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;
        sh:message "P4 datatype: the point at {?when} has a value for this field that is not a literal with the field's tss:datatype." ;
        sh:prefixes <https://w3id.org/tss/shapes/embedded> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT $this ?value ?when WHERE {
                ?source tss:hasField $this .
                $this tss:datatype ?datatype .
                { ?source tss:timeField $this ; tss:hasPoint ?point . ?point tss:time ?value . }
                UNION { $this a tss:ValueField . ?source tss:hasPoint ?point . ?point tss:value ?value . { ?point tss:field $this } UNION { FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?point tss:field ?anyField1 } ?source tss:hasField $this . $this a tss:ValueField . FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?source tss:hasField ?otherField1 . ?otherField1 a tss:ValueField . FILTER (?otherField1 != $this) } } }
                UNION { $this tss:property ?property . ?source tss:hasPoint ?point . ?point ?property ?value . }
                OPTIONAL { ?point tss:time ?time }
                BIND (COALESCE(STR(?time), "(no time)") AS ?when)
                FILTER (!isLiteral(?value) || (STR(?value) != "" && DATATYPE(?value) != ?datatype))
            }""" ;
    ] ;

    # P4: the text of the value is a valid value of its datatype (the XSD lexical forms).
    # A date or date-time must also be a real day: xsd:dateTime(...) gives no value for 30 February.
    sh:sparql [
        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;
        sh:message "P4 datatype: {?value} (the point at {?when}) is not a valid value of the field's tss:datatype." ;
        sh:prefixes <https://w3id.org/tss/shapes/embedded> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT $this ?value ?when WHERE {
                ?source tss:hasField $this .
                $this tss:datatype ?datatype .
                { ?source tss:timeField $this ; tss:hasPoint ?point . ?point tss:time ?value . }
                UNION { $this a tss:ValueField . ?source tss:hasPoint ?point . ?point tss:value ?value . { ?point tss:field $this } UNION { FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?point tss:field ?anyField1 } ?source tss:hasField $this . $this a tss:ValueField . FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?source tss:hasField ?otherField1 . ?otherField1 a tss:ValueField . FILTER (?otherField1 != $this) } } }
                UNION { $this tss:property ?property . ?source tss:hasPoint ?point . ?point ?property ?value . }
                FILTER (isLiteral(?value) && DATATYPE(?value) = ?datatype && STR(?value) != "")
                OPTIONAL { ?point tss:time ?time }
                BIND (COALESCE(STR(?time), "(no time)") AS ?when)
                BIND (STR(?value) AS ?text)
                BIND (xsd:dateTime(?text) AS ?moment)
                # A date: its day at midnight, without its timezone (xsd:dateTime("2021-03-04Z")
                # gives no value, although "2021-03-04Z" is a valid xsd:date)
                BIND (xsd:dateTime(CONCAT(REPLACE(?text, "(Z|[+-][0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2})$", ""), "T00:00:00")) AS ?day)
                FILTER (
                    (?datatype IN (xsd:double, xsd:float)
                        && !REGEX(?text, "^([+-]?(([0-9]+([.][0-9]*)?|[.][0-9]+)([eE][+-]?[0-9]+)?|INF)|NaN)$"))
                    || (?datatype = xsd:decimal
                        && !REGEX(?text, "^[+-]?([0-9]+([.][0-9]*)?|[.][0-9]+)$"))
                    || (?datatype IN (xsd:integer, xsd:long, xsd:int, xsd:short, xsd:byte)
                        && !REGEX(?text, "^[+-]?[0-9]+$"))
                    || (?datatype IN (xsd:nonNegativeInteger, xsd:unsignedLong, xsd:unsignedInt, xsd:unsignedShort, xsd:unsignedByte)
                        && !REGEX(?text, "^[+]?[0-9]+$"))
                    || (?datatype = xsd:positiveInteger
                        && !REGEX(?text, "^[+]?[0-9]*[1-9][0-9]*$"))
                    || (?datatype = xsd:nonPositiveInteger
                        && !REGEX(?text, "^(-[0-9]+|[+]?0+)$"))
                    || (?datatype = xsd:negativeInteger
                        && !REGEX(?text, "^-[0-9]*[1-9][0-9]*$"))
                    || (?datatype = xsd:boolean
                        && !REGEX(?text, "^(true|false|1|0)$"))
                    || (?datatype = xsd:dateTime
                        && (!REGEX(?text, "^-?[0-9]{4,}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}T[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}([.][0-9]+)?(Z|[+-][0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2})?$")
                            || !BOUND(?moment)))
                    # xsd:dateTimeStamp: an xsd:dateTime whose timezone can't be left out
                    || (?datatype = xsd:dateTimeStamp
                        && (!REGEX(?text, "^-?[0-9]{4,}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}T[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2}([.][0-9]+)?(Z|[+-][0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2})$")
                            || !BOUND(?moment)))
                    || (?datatype = xsd:date
                        && (!REGEX(?text, "^-?[0-9]{4,}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}(Z|[+-][0-9]{2}:[0-9]{2})?$")
                            || !BOUND(?day)))
                )
            }""" ;
    ] .


# --- P5: the expected range of a value field ---------------------------------------
# A shape of its own, because a SPARQL check takes its severity from its shape.
# tss:minimum and tss:maximum are informative: a reading outside them is still valid, so
# P5 only warns.

emb:FieldRangeShape a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetClass tss:Field, tss:ValueField, tss:ContextField ;
    sh:targetObjectsOf tss:hasField ;
    sh:severity sh:Warning ;

    # P5: a number is within the field's expected range. xsd:double(...) gives no value for a
    # text that is not a number; P4 reports those, so they are skipped here.
    sh:sparql [
        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;
        sh:message "P5 range: {?value} (the point at {?when}) is below the field's expected tss:minimum {?minimum}; the range is informative, so the value is still valid." ;
        sh:prefixes <https://w3id.org/tss/shapes/embedded> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT $this ?value ?when ?minimum WHERE {
                ?source tss:hasField $this .
                $this a tss:ValueField ; tss:minimum ?minimum .
                ?source tss:hasPoint ?point . ?point tss:value ?value .
                { ?point tss:field $this } UNION { FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?point tss:field ?anyField1 } ?source tss:hasField $this . $this a tss:ValueField . FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?source tss:hasField ?otherField1 . ?otherField1 a tss:ValueField . FILTER (?otherField1 != $this) } }
                OPTIONAL { ?point tss:time ?time }
                BIND (COALESCE(STR(?time), "(no time)") AS ?when)
                BIND (xsd:double(STR(?value)) AS ?number)
                FILTER (isNumeric(?value) && BOUND(?number) && ?number < ?minimum)
            }""" ;
    ] ;
    sh:sparql [
        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;
        sh:message "P5 range: {?value} (the point at {?when}) is above the field's expected tss:maximum {?maximum}; the range is informative, so the value is still valid." ;
        sh:prefixes <https://w3id.org/tss/shapes/embedded> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT $this ?value ?when ?maximum WHERE {
                ?source tss:hasField $this .
                $this a tss:ValueField ; tss:maximum ?maximum .
                ?source tss:hasPoint ?point . ?point tss:value ?value .
                { ?point tss:field $this } UNION { FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?point tss:field ?anyField1 } ?source tss:hasField $this . $this a tss:ValueField . FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?source tss:hasField ?otherField1 . ?otherField1 a tss:ValueField . FILTER (?otherField1 != $this) } }
                OPTIONAL { ?point tss:time ?time }
                BIND (COALESCE(STR(?time), "(no time)") AS ?when)
                BIND (xsd:double(STR(?value)) AS ?number)
                FILTER (isNumeric(?value) && BOUND(?number) && ?number > ?maximum)
            }""" ;
    ] .


# --- P6: every property of a point is read --------------------------------------
# A shape of its own, because a SPARQL check takes its severity from its shape.
# A point states tss:field, tss:time, tss:value and the properties of describing fields: their
# tss:property, or the default property made from their column name. Any other property (a
# typo, rdf:type: a point states no type) is not read, so its values are lost.

emb:PointPropertiesShape a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetClass tss:EmbeddedRDFSource ;
    sh:severity sh:Warning ;
    sh:sparql [
        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;
        sh:message "P6 properties: a point has the property {?value}, which is not tss:field, tss:time, tss:value or the property of a describing field of the source, so its values are not read." ;
        sh:prefixes <https://w3id.org/tss/shapes/embedded> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT DISTINCT $this ?value WHERE {
                $this tss:hasPoint ?point .
                ?point ?value ?any .
                FILTER (?value NOT IN (tss:field, tss:time, tss:value))
                FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this tss:hasField ?describing . ?describing tss:property ?value }
                # The default property of a describing field: the document IRI, '#', its column name
                FILTER NOT EXISTS {
                    $this tss:hasField ?default .
                    ?default tss:describesField ?described ; tss:columnName ?name .
                    FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?default tss:property ?property }
                    FILTER (STRENDS(STR(?value), CONCAT("#", ENCODE_FOR_URI(?name))))
                }
            }""" ;
    ] .

# --- Optional field summaries --------------------------------------------------
# No sh:minCount: neither the summary nor any of its attributes is mandatory.
# Validate supplied values without requiring a complete summary or scanning the data.

emb:SummaryShape a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetObjectsOf tss:summary ;
    sh:nodeKind sh:BlankNodeOrIRI ;
    sh:property [
        sh:name "Q1 from" ;
        sh:group emb:NotAllowed ;
        sh:path tss:from ;
        sh:maxCount 0 ;
        sh:message "Q1 not allowed: a summary has no window of its own; it covers the source's time window, so it has no tss:from." ;
    ] ;
    sh:property [
        sh:name "Q2 until" ;
        sh:group emb:NotAllowed ;
        sh:path tss:until ;
        sh:maxCount 0 ;
        sh:message "Q2 not allowed: a summary has no window of its own; it covers the source's time window, so it has no tss:until." ;
    ] ;
    sh:property [
        sh:name "Q3 missing-value policy" ;
        sh:group emb:Optional ;
        sh:path tss:missingValuePolicy ;
        sh:maxCount 1 ;
        sh:nodeKind sh:IRI ;
        sh:message "tss:missingValuePolicy must be one IRI, such as tss:ExcludeEmptyValues, when supplied." ;
    ] ;
    sh:property [
        sh:name "Q4 count" ;
        sh:group emb:Optional ;
        sh:path tss:count ;
        sh:maxCount 1 ;
        sh:datatype xsd:integer ;
        sh:minInclusive 0 ;
        sh:message "tss:count must be one non-negative xsd:integer when supplied." ;
    ] ;
    sh:property [
        sh:name "Q5 missing" ;
        sh:group emb:Optional ;
        sh:path tss:missing ;
        sh:maxCount 1 ;
        sh:datatype xsd:integer ;
        sh:minInclusive 0 ;
        sh:message "tss:missing must be one non-negative xsd:integer when supplied." ;
    ] ;
    sh:property [
        sh:name "Q6 first time" ;
        sh:group emb:Optional ;
        sh:path tss:firstTime ;
        sh:maxCount 1 ;
        sh:or ( [ sh:datatype xsd:dateTime ] [ sh:datatype xsd:dateTimeStamp ] ) ;
        sh:message "tss:firstTime must be one xsd:dateTime (with a timezone) when supplied." ;
    ] ;
    sh:property [
        sh:name "Q7 last time" ;
        sh:group emb:Optional ;
        sh:path tss:lastTime ;
        sh:maxCount 1 ;
        sh:or ( [ sh:datatype xsd:dateTime ] [ sh:datatype xsd:dateTimeStamp ] ) ;
        sh:message "tss:lastTime must be one xsd:dateTime (with a timezone) when supplied." ;
    ] ;
    sh:property [
        sh:name "Q8 observed minimum" ;
        sh:group emb:Optional ;
        sh:path tss:observedMinimum ;
        sh:maxCount 1 ;
        sh:or ( [ sh:datatype xsd:integer ] [ sh:datatype xsd:decimal ] [ sh:datatype xsd:double ] [ sh:datatype xsd:float ] ) ;
        sh:message "tss:observedMinimum must be one number when supplied." ;
    ] ;
    sh:property [
        sh:name "Q9 observed maximum" ;
        sh:group emb:Optional ;
        sh:path tss:observedMaximum ;
        sh:maxCount 1 ;
        sh:or ( [ sh:datatype xsd:integer ] [ sh:datatype xsd:decimal ] [ sh:datatype xsd:double ] [ sh:datatype xsd:float ] ) ;
        sh:message "tss:observedMaximum must be one number when supplied." ;
    ] ;
    sh:property [
        sh:name "Q10 mean" ;
        sh:group emb:Optional ;
        sh:path tss:mean ;
        sh:maxCount 1 ;
        sh:or ( [ sh:datatype xsd:integer ] [ sh:datatype xsd:decimal ] [ sh:datatype xsd:double ] [ sh:datatype xsd:float ] ) ;
        sh:message "tss:mean must be one number when supplied." ;
    ] ;
    sh:property [
        sh:name "Q11 median" ;
        sh:group emb:Optional ;
        sh:path tss:median ;
        sh:maxCount 1 ;
        sh:or ( [ sh:datatype xsd:integer ] [ sh:datatype xsd:decimal ] [ sh:datatype xsd:double ] [ sh:datatype xsd:float ] ) ;
        sh:message "tss:median must be one number when supplied." ;
    ] ;
    sh:property [
        sh:name "Q12 generated at time" ;
        sh:group emb:Optional ;
        sh:path tss:generatedAtTime ;
        sh:maxCount 1 ;
        sh:or ( [ sh:datatype xsd:dateTime ] [ sh:datatype xsd:dateTimeStamp ] ) ;
        sh:message "tss:generatedAtTime must be one xsd:dateTime (with a timezone) when supplied." ;
    ] .


# --- S26: no stored summary on a growing source ---------------------------------
# A source that does not state tss:immutable true is growing: points may still be added, so a
# summary would be outdated by the next Write, and its description does not change while it
# grows. A writer adds the summaries when it ends the source, together with tss:immutable true.

emb:GrowingSourceSummaryShape a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetClass tss:EmbeddedJSONSource, tss:EmbeddedRDFSource ;
    sh:sparql [
        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;
        sh:message "S26 summary of a growing source: field {?value} has a tss:summary, but the source does not state tss:immutable true. Only a field of an immutable source has a stored summary." ;
        sh:prefixes <https://w3id.org/tss/shapes/embedded> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT $this ?value WHERE {
                $this tss:hasField ?value .
                ?value tss:summary ?summary .
                FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this tss:immutable ?immutable . FILTER (?immutable = true) }
            }""" ;
    ] .


# --- S29: a source has at least one value field ----------------------------------
# A shape of its own, because a SPARQL check takes its severity from its shape. A source
# SHOULD have a value field: a source without one holds no readings.

emb:ValueFieldShape a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetClass tss:EmbeddedJSONSource, tss:EmbeddedRDFSource ;
    sh:severity sh:Warning ;
    sh:sparql [
        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;
        sh:message "S29 value field: the source has no tss:ValueField, so it holds no readings." ;
        sh:prefixes <https://w3id.org/tss/shapes/embedded> ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT $this WHERE {
                FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this tss:hasField ?field . ?field a tss:ValueField }
            }""" ;
    ] .
